 R←Test_OnWait_003(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP
⍝ Exercise "SetOnWait": the function established must not be called when automation answers
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 ∆OnWaitCalls←⍬
 ∆OnWaitSpy C.SetOnWait 0
 C.AddAutomation'YesOrNo' 'Sure@' 'y'
 C.AddAutomation'Select' 'Pick@' 2
 C.AddAutomation'Pause' 'Wait@' ''
 C.AddAutomation'AskForText' 'Name@' 'John'
 C.AddAutomation'AskForNumber' 'Copies@' 3

 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠C.YesOrNo'Sure@Are you sure?'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2≠'Pick@Pick one'C.Select'First' 'Second' 'Third'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠C.Pause'Wait@Should not stop'
 →T.GoToTidyUp'John'≢({1}C.AskForText)'Name@Your name'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 3≠({1}C.AskForNumber)'Copies@Number of copies'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 5≠+/C.∆Automation[;4]
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠≢∆OnWaitCalls

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 C.Cleanup
 C.UnsetOnWait
 ⎕EX'∆OnWaitCalls'
⍝Done
